WEBVTT

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.680
That prisoner is gorgeous.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.710
You may not know since you're new...

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.300
But that prisoner is a cyber terrorist.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.620
One of the Knights of Hanoi.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.360
What?  That hacker organization?

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:28.550
Yeah.  She's one of the main 
culprits who destroyed LINK VRAINS.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.580
But LINK VRAINS is virtual reality.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.520
This is a special prison for felons.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.460
Is that big enough of a crime 
to be locked up in here?

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.520
She used a computer virus 
to put people in danger.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.490
She's facing various charges.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:54.270
SOL Technologies filed many charges, 
so she won't be leaving anytime soon.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:59.180
So I can keep staring at 
her until then?  Nice!

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.040
Hey!  Take your job seriously!

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.120
Yes sir...

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:25.280
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:32.090
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:39.370
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:45.940
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:52.710
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:59.950
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:06.630
I want to share your pain

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.550
An Ignis who named itself Flame.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:42.080
And its duelist, Soulburner.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.180
So there's a new Playmaker.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.860
What?  Is this a joke?

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:06.200
While we were creating the Tower of Hanoi, 
someone destroyed the Cyberse World.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.340
How unexpected.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:13.180
Someone other than us wants 
to destroy the Cyberse?

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.940
Did that person take the Ignis?

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.710
Not necessarily.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.320
The duelist named Soulburner 
has the fire Ignis.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:31.890
It's likely the Ignis we 
want to kill have scattered.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.300
How troublesome.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:42.480
The duelist working with the 
Ignis must be like me, a Lost-

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.440
I've already checked him out.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.140
His real name is Takeru Homura.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.100
A Lost Incident victim.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:58.790
The fire Ignis escaped from the Cyberse 
and went to the person it's based on.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.080
But Revolver, no Ignis has come to me.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.260
Of course not.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:10.280
The Knights of Hanoi want to kill the Ignis.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:15.710
If you're one of us, an 
Ignis won't come to you.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.280
That's true.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.170
Yusaku Fujiki and Takeru Homura.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.070
We've identified their location.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:29.560
We should act immediately 
and take the two Ignis-

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:30.380
No!

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:36.020
What happens in the network, 
we take care of in the network!

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.760
That's how I do things!

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.760
Stay away from them in the real world!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.440
I apologize.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:51.200
And we know more than anyone that 
Playmaker won't be easily defeated.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.200
Yes.  Fully.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.100
No need to be impatient.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.170
Let's just observe the Ignis for now.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:04.650
The two Ignis may contact the other Ignis.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.880
So let them go on purpose.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:14.630
Yes.  And I'm more intrigued by the mystery 
duelist that Playmaker is pursuing.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:17.870
Yes.  His name is Bohman.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.070
Who are you?

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:32.980
Bohman stole consciousness data from Jin 
- Shoichi Kusanagi's younger brother.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:37.200
Jin Kusanagi is also a victim 
of the Lost Incident.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:42.060
After the Lost Incident, he was 
hospitalized in a facility.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:45.800
He's a victim of our crime.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:48.800
It's not your fault, Revolver.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:53.020
Jin's brother Shoichi is Playmaker's partner.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:58.040
So Playmaker won't stay quiet.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:01.040
Have you learned anything about him?

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:04.050
Unfortunately, nothing.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:10.360
We do know his avatar is 
a high-quality program.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:14.510
Looking at the security 
footage at Jin's facility...

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:19.310
...he stole consciousness 
data directly from his body.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:23.530
His method is superior to 
Baira's computer virus.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:28.500
So the one who created this 
avatar is someone special.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:32.970
Yes.  And we should be most careful about...

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:34.350
Link Spell?

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:39.080
I activate the Link Spell, Judgment Arrows!

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:43.090
A spell card with Link Markers...

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:48.730
This card may become a big threat to us.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:52.090
I've never seen a card like that before.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:56.840
Can he be SOL Technologies' assassin?

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.300
Most likely not.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.210
Brother, we're almost there.  Hang on.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:08.270
Jin Kusanagi's data is ours.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:11.010
Stop joking!  Why are you doing this?

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.020
Something unbelievable will happen soon.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:15.750
Stay tuned.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:22.820
According to SOL Technologies' logs, Bohman 
escaped through that mysterious gate.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:26.240
The gate was located here.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:29.220
But before Bohman went inside...

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:34.810
...the logs say SOL Technologies' research 
team entered the gate and faced distress.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:40.480
Meaning SOL Technologies can't control this.

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:45.970
And SOL Technologies' bounty hunters, 
including Go Onizuka,

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:48.490
have begun searching for the Ignis.

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:51.690
And they didn't know about 
the gate's existence.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:55.900
I can't believe SOL Technologies hired him.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:57.900
Go Onizuka...

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:00.420
He doesn't care about prestige or rank.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.630
He's always looking for a fight.

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:05.840
I'm Soulburner!

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.870
Who are you?  Don't interfere!

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.880
Please calm down, senpai!

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.120
But I have one too.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.090
What?  Then you're also...

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:22.650
Feel like dueling me now?

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.690
Fine.  I'll take you on.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:26.580
All right!

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.350
I activate my Skill!

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:30.330
Dinowrestle Revolution!

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:35.290
From my deck, I activate the Field 
Spell, World Dino Wrestling!

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:41.410
When my Dinowrestler attacks 
your monster, it gains 200 ATK!

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.370
Dinowrestler?

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:46.370
He's not using his Gouki Deck anymore.

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:49.260
So he's evolved a lot.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:52.250
It's impossible to predict this duel.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:55.380
He already surpassed our expectations.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:58.360
Go Onizuka is impressive!

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.000
I don't care about the glory of the past.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:03.520
Playmaker...

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:09.430
Until I defeat him, I can't 
take one step forward.

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:12.840
Appear, my circuit!

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:14.770
Link Summon!

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:21.510
Appear, Link 3 Dinowrestler King T Wrextle!

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:26.520
Take this!  Jurassic Howl!

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:35.420
Go Onizuka...  I want to duel the real you.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:39.590
And I'll fight the real you and win!

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:44.360
Because I have a reason why I can't lose too!

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.970
My time has remained stopped since that day.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:57.970
Your Mom and Dad searched for you every day.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:03.890
And they were in an accident.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:09.770
After losing my parents, all I 
had left were my grandparents...

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:13.390
...and dueling, which I 
vowed never to do again!

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:21.510
To make time move again, 
all I can do is duel!

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:23.810
I activate my Skill!

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:32.850
By dropping my LP to 100, I draw one 
card for every 1000 LP that I paid!

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:37.280
Show a miracle!  Burning Draw!

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:39.950
Ritual Summon!

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:42.950
Rise, Level 8!

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.670
Jade wings clad in flames!

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:49.160
Salamangreat Emerald Eagle!

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:54.640
Battle!

00:10:55.240 --> 00:11:01.460
Salamangreat Emerald Eagle attacks 
Dinowrestler King T Wrextle!

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:05.500
Emerald Overload!

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.580
Well done!

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:19.050
He defeated Go Onizuka.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:23.690
We must not underestimate Soulburner.

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:25.860
Playmaker and Soulburner.

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:29.110
And Go Onizuka pursues them.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:32.970
Everyone headed to the mysterious gate.

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:38.820
If SOL Technologies was the mastermind...

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.880
...Bohman wouldn't need to 
escape through the gate.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:48.610
I see.  And SOL Technologies is careless.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:51.680
There's a new gate they can't control...

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:56.690
...but they conceal its existence 
and open a new LINK VRAINS.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:00.600
The public never knows the truth.

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:04.960
There's always an eerie 
darkness in the shadows.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.340
I'll destroy SOL Technologies 
to avenge my father.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:12.570
And those obsessed with money!

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:15.990
We've been analyzing the gate-

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.810
It's already finished.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:21.960
An Ignis algorithm created the gate.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:23.430
Ignis?

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:27.680
So there's no connection to SOL Technologies.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:32.070
No one working there has the skills.

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:35.400
But there's one man that intrigues me.

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:40.370
SOL Technologies hired a 
man named Blood Shepherd.

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:45.400
Among cyber treasure hunters, he's infamous 
for his excellent hacking techniques...

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:51.220
...and doing whatever it 
takes to capture his prey.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.920
I'll count to three.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.320
Link Summon!

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.400
Deploy!

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:03.030
Link 3 Battledrone General!

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:08.300
Happy birthday, Mom.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:09.920
Thank you.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:15.040
Is this safe?  There's no driver.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.040
Don't be silly.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.540
This taxi is loaded with the latest AI.

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:22.250
Incredible, right?

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:27.790
This AI system selects the most 
precise, shortest and safest route.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.250
An accident?

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:32.260
Avoiding accident.  Changing route.

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:35.190
Hey!  What's wrong?

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:38.770
Damn!  Duck, Mom!

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:44.970
Your mother's spinal cord is greatly damaged.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.980
She'll never stand again.

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:51.440
And your right arm...

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:56.410
Blood Shepherd...  I've 
heard rumors about him.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:14:00.580
An AI derailed his life.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:04.320
There's no one who hates AIs more than him.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:10.320
But it's unconfirmed whether he has the 
intellect and skills that rival Dr. Kogami.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:13.930
Only a few can solve an Ignis algorithm.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:19.770
Only my father, me and the Ignis.

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:22.510
I see.  So the gate's creator is...

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:24.740
Yes.  The Ignis.

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:30.720
So they took Jin Kusanagi's 
data to lure out Playmaker?

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.360
Playmaker!

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:37.920
Is that the gate?

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.830
He must've gone through that.

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:44.070
Let's go!

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:50.140
It's too early to reach that conclusion.

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:56.240
But they may have formed a secret 
party on the other side of the gate.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:15:02.310
Then I'd like to participate 
in the next party.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:09.430
If the Ignis begin creating their own world, 
it'll be a second or third secret Cyberse.

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:14.060
That would make it even 
harder to find the Ignis.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:17.300
They're evolving faster than anticipated.

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:23.730
As my father predicted, they may 
have already started a new plan.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:31.610
And we must be wary of Playmaker's growth 
as a duelist, since he is helping the Ignis.

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:34.580
In addition to Link Summoning...

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:40.860
From my hand, I activate the 
Ritual Spell, Cynet Ritual!

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:43.190
A Ritual Spell?

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:50.110
I tribute monsters from my hand and field 
whose total Level equals or surpasses...

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:55.680
...the Cyberse Ritual Monster that 
I'm Ritual Summoning from my hand!

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:03.110
I tribute Level 4 Cyberse Wizard 
and Level 3 Defcon Bird!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:09.190
The contract has been made.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:14.320
The sage who wields dark power 
inherits these two souls!

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:16.220
Ritual Summon!

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:22.030
Rise, Cyberse Magician!

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:27.200
A Ritual Summon that unites 
with Link Summon...

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:30.270
I'll finish you with this!

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:31.970
That's...

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:35.620
I activate the spell card, Cynet Fusion!

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:41.950
I send Fusion Material from my hand and 
field to the graveyard to summon a Fusion Monster!

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:49.430
I fuse Clock Wyvern, Shootingcode 
Talker and Clock Spartoi!

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:50.860
Fusion!

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:55.560
The strong ones gather 
before its grand wings!

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:58.130
Become a new legend!

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:59.640
Fusion Summon!

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:09.070
Come out!  Cyberse Clock Dragon!

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:19.820
And he's mastered Fusion Summoning.

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:25.890
Playmaker will definitely 
stand in our way again.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:29.370
He truly is our greatest enemy.

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:33.300
We must form a counterplan immediately.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:38.470
But before that, there's 
one thing we must do.

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:39.620
Let's go.

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:54.290
Ryoken.

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:57.530
We're ready.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:04.900
She's in a state-of-the-art prison 
dedicated to big-time criminals.

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:07.900
It runs on an auto-lock computer system.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:12.870
They say escape is impossible 
from the world's toughest prison.

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:16.550
But for us, that facility is full of holes.

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:21.880
We just needed time to rewrite the system.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:26.350
Since the Tower of Hanoi, 
it took three whole months.

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:31.090
Any chance that security updates 
detected us during these months?

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:38.610
None.  We already sent a powerful virus to 
the station in charge to act as a dummy.

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:41.940
They're super busy dealing with it.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:46.670
These are the security cameras' blind 
spots and the guards' patrol routes.

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:48.950
The plan is underway.

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:52.250
Dummy footage will play on 
all the security cameras.

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:55.170
Doors along the route will be unlocked.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:01.890
During this time, we'll be ghosts.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:05.790
But there's a 20-minute time limit.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.260
That's plenty.

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.260
Because we're only coming and going.

00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:17.440
She's beautiful.

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:21.340
I don't care if she's a villain.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:28.010
I was waiting for you.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:30.750
Ryoken.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.720
Sorry to keep you waiting, Dr. Taki.

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:37.050
I knew you'd come.

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:39.960
Is a new fight starting?

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:44.560
Yes.  We're heading to a new destiny.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:55.250
She vanished!

00:19:58.300 --> 00:19:59.540
She's not here!

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:02.010
She escaped!

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:07.590
The time is now.

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:12.110
The Knights of Hanoi are back!

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:25.140
Why did Windy's gate disappear?

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:27.590
That's what I want to know.

00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:30.600
Any clue leading to Bohman is now gone.

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:33.620
So we have to wait for him to approach us.

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:37.460
He always does what he wants.

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.620
But no point losing my cool.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:42.360
He'll eventually reopen it.

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.420
Hope so.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:47.800
Did something happen to Windy?

00:20:48.610 --> 00:20:50.010
Or...

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:55.460
A message from Kusanagi.

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:58.040
Something must have happened.  Let's go!

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:00.440
You're not gonna look at the message?

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:05.300
Kusanagi!  What happened?

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:07.380
Yusaku, look at this.

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:11.740
Baira escaped?

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:14.780
No way!  She escaped?

00:21:14.780 --> 00:21:16.170
Can this be...

